# Code owners: the maintainer owns every path .github/risk-assessment.yml rates
# high (docs/risk-tiers.md): CI and gates, gate tooling, build and
# dependencies, the app manifest, agent instructions, and container
# configuration. A pull request that touches one requests his review, and the
# merge queue leaves it for him to merge. Low- and medium-risk paths have no
# owner, so their PRs merge through the queue once the required checks pass.
#
# Keep this file and the high-risk rules in step: CodeownersTest in tests/
# fails if a tracked file is high risk but unowned, or owned but not high risk.
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax: a leading `/` anchors to the repository root,
# and a pattern without a `/` matches at any depth.

# CI gates, review rubric, rulesets, the risk rules, and this file itself.
/.github/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Gate tooling: CI scripts and the tests that pin the workflows.
/scripts/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/tests/                             @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Build and dependencies (supply chain): version catalog, wrapper, build scripts.
/gradle/                            @Tim-van-Oudheusden
*.gradle.kts                        @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/gradle.properties                  @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/gradlew                            @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/gradlew.bat                        @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# App permissions and the HOME intent filter.
/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml   @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Line endings, text/binary handling and diff/merge drivers for every file.
/.gitattributes                     @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Agent instructions and governance.
